 The matrix corresponding to a clockwise rotation by an angle $\theta$ is given by:
\[
\begin{pmatrix}
\cos \theta & \sin \theta \\
-\sin \theta & \cos \theta
\end{pmatrix}
\]
For $\theta = 45^\circ$, we have $\cos 45^\circ = \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}$ and $\sin 45^\circ = \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}$. Therefore, the matrix is:
\[
\begin{pmatrix}
\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} & \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} \\
-\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} & \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}
\end{pmatrix}
\]
